  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 320 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe Heat Advisory is valid through Friday evening. The synoptic high \npressure does not look to release its grip on the southeast and \nsouthern Plains this week, in fact retrograding slightly to more \nfirmly place the Ozarks under its influence. Highs are expected in \nthe 90s the remainder of the week, somewhere between 10 to even 20 \ndegrees above normal for this time of year. Lows in the upper 60s to \nlow 70s are also much higher than normal lows in the mid 50s. A \nlarge swath of the area is under Extreme HeatRisk with almost \neverywhere under at least Major.\n\nA strong low pressure that is actually sitting over the Pacific \nnorthwest currently may be the bowling ball we need to knock the \npersistent high pressure out of its place. Ensembles are suggesting \na synoptic pattern change by early next week with a frontal passage, \ncooler temperatures, and maybe even some widespread rain. While \nthere is uncertainty on exact details at this lead time, there \ndoes appear to be some hope on the horizon with even 75th \npercentile highs in the 80s and widespread PoPs 30-50%.",
